1
00:00:38,649 --> 00:00:39,649
Hey! Hey, no!

2
00:00:42,800 --> 00:00:45,760
No!
No! No!

3
00:00:46,780 --> 00:00:47,780
No!

4
00:02:20,100 --> 00:02:21,100
Excuse me?

5
00:02:22,040 --> 00:02:23,200
Excuse me,
sir?

6
00:02:24,400 --> 00:02:25,400
Excuse me?

7
00:02:26,900 --> 00:02:28,560
Oh, come on.

8
00:02:30,440 --> 00:02:31,793
You have a moment, sir?

9
00:02:32,440 --> 00:02:36,440
I'm kind of in the middle
of something here, yes, thank you.

10
00:02:36,880 --> 00:02:39,057
I've come a long way for you, Franck.

11
00:02:49,420 --> 00:02:50,479
My name is Victor.

12
00:02:52,540 --> 00:02:53,540
Hi.

13
00:02:54,980 --> 00:02:55,980
And you are...

14
00:02:57,860 --> 00:02:58,860
you are Franck.

15
00:03:00,500 --> 00:03:03,736
But you are so much more
than just a sheep, aren't you?

16
00:03:04,740 --> 00:03:05,740
Oh yeah?

17
00:03:06,760 --> 00:03:08,020
How would you know?

18
00:03:10,380 --> 00:03:12,851
Look at you. You're an adventurer, Franck.

19
00:03:14,000 --> 00:03:16,680
Just like me, you're
a lone wolf.

20
00:03:18,680 --> 00:03:21,800
Tell me, does one choose
to be alone?

21
00:03:23,000 --> 00:03:24,020
No, one doesn't.

22
00:03:25,200 --> 00:03:27,377
One doesn't even choose to be a wolf.

23
00:03:29,980 --> 00:03:30,980
Or does one?

24
00:03:35,460 --> 00:03:36,580
Well, Mr...

25
00:03:38,240 --> 00:03:38,900
Hector.

26
00:03:38,900 --> 00:03:39,900
Victor, Victor.

27
00:03:40,040 --> 00:03:41,920
I don't know what you're on about,

28
00:03:41,920 --> 00:03:45,300
but I'm just a sheep
minding its own business.

29
00:03:46,620 --> 00:03:48,780
And I suggest you do the same.

30
00:03:49,440 --> 00:03:51,852
No, no, no, no, Franck, wait, wait, wait.

31
00:03:52,000 --> 00:03:54,380
No, this is not
the way.

32
00:03:54,620 --> 00:03:57,326
Just give me one
minute of your precious time.

33
00:03:58,540 --> 00:04:00,140
Precious time?

34
00:04:02,100 --> 00:04:05,600
Yeah, just give me one minute.
You would have one more minute,

35
00:04:05,600 --> 00:04:06,600
wouldn't you?

36
00:04:08,400 --> 00:04:09,400
Okay, half.

37
00:04:10,100 --> 00:04:11,100
Half a minute.

38
00:04:25,620 --> 00:04:26,620
I knew it.

39
00:04:28,080 --> 00:04:29,140
I
knew it.

40
00:04:30,380 --> 00:04:34,520
Ah, you will not regret this.
The adventures you will have,

41
00:04:35,840 --> 00:04:38,020
all the lives you ever wanted,

42
00:04:39,580 --> 00:04:40,992
all you've been missing.

43
00:04:41,740 --> 00:04:42,820
Here,
this is

44
00:04:43,500 --> 00:04:45,840
the best product we have
in store:

45
00:04:47,180 --> 00:04:48,360
variable spin speed,

46
00:04:48,580 --> 00:04:53,340
excellent tumble performance in one
handy device. Squeaky clean.

47
00:04:57,180 --> 00:04:58,180
Well,

48
00:04:59,080 --> 00:05:00,257
this better be good.

49
00:05:01,580 --> 00:05:03,800
It took me ages to tie that rope

50
00:05:04,920 --> 00:05:06,620
with my fucking hooves.

51
00:05:07,400 --> 00:05:08,812
No more need for hooves.

52
00:05:09,240 --> 00:05:10,652
No more sheepy business.

53
00:05:13,720 --> 00:05:14,680
Time flies.

54
00:05:14,680 --> 00:05:16,739
Wait, wait, wait, wait, wait, wait.

55
00:05:16,920 --> 00:05:20,920
How does this thing work?
I mean, how do I make it work?

56
00:05:21,140 --> 00:05:23,900
No, you don't.
I just turned it on for you.

57
00:05:26,200 --> 00:05:27,240
When can I go?

58
00:05:29,060 --> 00:05:30,220
Where can I go?

59
00:05:30,260 --> 00:05:32,202
We will pick you up. Don't worry.

60
00:05:32,340 --> 00:05:35,260
Just stay here,
in this exact place.

61
00:05:35,260 --> 00:05:36,880
Don't move.
Just wait.

62
00:05:38,500 --> 00:05:39,500
That's it?

63
00:05:41,140 --> 00:05:42,140
Hey!

64
00:05:42,720 --> 00:05:43,720
Hey!

65
00:05:44,360 --> 00:05:45,760
Wait, mister!

66
00:05:47,280 --> 00:05:48,280
Casper!

67
00:05:49,340 --> 00:05:50,360
Hector, whatever!
